---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | ImageLab"
  description="How ImageLab protects your privacy through 100% local browser processing with zero server image uploads."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 space-y-8 animate-fade-up">
    <header>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400 mb-2">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 mt-2">Last updated: November 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="studio-card rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">1. Zero Server Image Uploads</h2>
        <p>
          Every image conversion, compression, resize, crop, watermark, PDF creation, background
          removal, and AI enhancement runs strictly inside your web browser using WebAssembly,
          WebGPU, and browser Canvas APIs. Your photos, signatures, and documents are never
          uploaded to or stored on ImageLab servers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">2. Third-Party CDN Model Downloads</h2>
        <p>
          When you choose to run our on-device AI tools (AI Background Remover or AI Photo
          Enhancer), your browser fetches the open-source AI model weights from public CDNs
          (such as jsDelivr, Hugging Face, or IMG.LY) and caches them locally in your browser.
          Only the model files are downloaded; your personal photos are never sent to those CDNs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">3. Local Storage & Preferences</h2>
        <p>
          ImageLab stores your Dark/Light theme preference in your browser’s
          <code>localStorage</code>. We do not require accounts or collect personal profiles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">4. Hosting & Future Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which may process standard network access logs
          (such as IP address and user agent) for security and DDoS protection. If advertising
          partners (such as Google AdSense) are enabled in the future, they may use cookies
          according to their respective privacy policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">5. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions regarding privacy? Reach out via our <a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
